  "slug": "channel-calcium-423b",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published study couple mechanical, transport and ECM processes within single computational frameworks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational formulation of cell behavior in which mechanical, transport, or microenvironmental coupling is explicit within one framework. A hybrid agent-based and PDE model treats intranasal neural stem cell migration in glioblastoma under IL-10 and CXCL12 pretreatment and radiotherapy. A system-theoretic analysis of Extended Cellular Potts Models couples tumor cell dynamics to ECM degradation and provides convergence bounds. Multispecies transport models of gasdermin-perforated cells reveal non-canonical Donnan states and pore-clustering effects on osmotic gradients. A dimensionless surface PDE solved by evolving surface FEM couples plasma and nuclear envelope membrane mechanics in confined migration. What is new is the integration of distinct physical or biochemical processes within a single model. These works differ in scale and in whether results are analytical or simulation-based, so the shared element is coupling rather than a common method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
